  "facts": {
    "intro": "A clear tank holds the blue\u2011tinged liquid, showing the amount remaining as the sprayer is used.",
    "reveal": "Pressing the thumb lever pulls the pump plunger back, compressing the return spring inside the barrel.",
    "step1": "When the lever is released, the spring pushes the plunger forward, closing the valve at the top of the tank.",
    "step2": "The forward motion forces a small amount of liquid up through the internal tube toward the mist nozzle.",
    "step3": "At the nozzle, the liquid meets a tiny aperture that atomizes it into a fine mist as it exits.",
    "step4": "The mist stream shoots out of the spout, coating plants evenly while the tank gradually empties.",
    "hold": "If the trigger is held down, the spring continues to drive the plunger, delivering a steady stream until the tank empties.",
    "payoff": "Releasing the trigger lets the spring reset, readying the sprayer for the next precise burst of mist."
  }
